@startuml view-2
title View 2 - Report lifecycle: states and the data persisted at each step

[*] --> submitted : Citizen creates report\nINSERT reports (current_status=submitted,\ncitizen_editable=true, operator_id=NULL,\nlocation, category, optional image)\n[ReportService.registerNewReport]

submitted --> assigned : Operator updates status\nUPDATE reports (current_status, citizen_editable=false, operator_id)\nINSERT status_updates(new_status=assigned, operator_id)\nthen INSERT notifications (notifiable)
assigned --> in_progress : Operator updates status\nUPDATE reports (current_status)\nINSERT status_updates(new_status=in_progress, operator_id)\nno notification
in_progress --> resolved : Operator updates status\nUPDATE reports (current_status)\nINSERT status_updates(new_status=resolved, operator_id)\nthen INSERT notifications (notifiable)
resolved --> [*] : terminal\nIllegalStateException on further update

note right of submitted
  isStatusNotifiable = false
  Citizen-editable flag = true
end note
note right of assigned
  isStatusNotifiable = true
end note
note right of in_progress
  isStatusNotifiable = false
end note
note right of resolved
  isStatusNotifiable = true
end note

note bottom
  Side activity at any state (operator only): InternalNote added via
  Report.addInternalNote -> INSERT internal_notes(text, created_date, report_id, operator_id).
  Notes do not change the state.
  Status updates and notes are appended, never updated or deleted (history is append-only).
  Observed in code: ReportService.updateReportStatus persists the report and its StatusUpdate
  in one merge (one transaction); the Notification is saved afterwards in a separate
  transaction (ReportStatusUpdateController -> NotificationController), so a failure
  between them leaves the state change without a notification.
  Note: the notifiable test (Report.isCurrentStatusNotifiable) uses the report's
  current state, not the newStatus argument passed in.
end note
@enduml
